2026-09-13 — Enhanced: bidding reworked so a bid is the whole offer

A bid now carries the price, the delivery costs and the taxes together, and
the form follows how the auction will be handed out:

  * price + freight/packaging/other + taxes, submitted as one bid; taxes are
    compulsory on a delivered-price auction (0% allowed, but it must be typed)
  * awarded to one supplier  -> the whole auction is bid for as one lot, costs
    quoted once for the consignment, ranked on the grand total
  * awarded item by item     -> each item bid for on its own, with its own
    costs and taxes, and the button names the item
  * a bidder can take back only their most recent bid; the one before it
    stands again. The buyer keeps the power to strike out any bid.
  * "Your bids on this auction": every submission kept verbatim, with the
    prices and tax rates as typed and the exact time each went in

Preceded by the six-round deep check (rounds 1-6), which found and fixed
seven real defects and left roughly 1,300 permanent checks behind it.
